{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nDuring the 0.13.0 release (ticket hyperbolic-pernicious-drongo, Gerrit change 2385 merged as\n4dafd36d2aa1), release.yml's \"Publish to MCP Registry\" job failed all 5 retry attempts with:\n\n    Error: publish failed: server returned status 422: {\"title\":\"Unprocessable Entity\",\"status\":422,\n    \"detail\":\"validation failed\",\"errors\":[{\"message\":\"expected length <= 100\",\n    \"location\":\"body.description\",\"value\":\"Rebar can block work until an AI plan review passes,\n    require signed completion verification before close, and reconcile its event-sourced ticket\n    record with Jira across CLI, Python, and MCP.\"}]}\n\nserver.json's top-level \"description\" field (190 chars, identical to pyproject.toml's description)\nexceeds the registry's <= 100 char schema constraint. PyPI publish and the GitHub Release both\nsucceeded (irreversible, already live for 0.13.0); only the MCP Registry publish step failed.\nNothing in local CI (make lint, scripts/check_server_manifest.py, release_guards.py) catches this\nlocally -- the 422 was only ever surfaced by the live registry's remote validation during the\nrelease, after PyPI was already published.\n\n## Plan\n- Shorten server.json's top-level description to <= 100 chars (keep pyproject.toml's longer,\n  descriptive form -- there is no lockstep guard requiring the two to match, confirmed by\n  inspection of scripts/release_guards.py and scripts/check_server_manifest.py).\n- Add a local guard (check_mcp_registry_description function + a \"mcp-registry-description\" CLI\n  subcommand in scripts/release_guards.py, alongside the existing check_version_lockstep /\n  check_env_protection helpers) asserting server.json's top-level description is <= 100 chars,\n  with a unit test in tests/unit/test_release_guards.py.\n- WIRE the new guard into release.yml's \"Authorize release source\" job (a new \"Guard — server.json\n  description fits the MCP Registry schema\" step, immediately after the existing version-lockstep\n  guard step) so a future release fails BEFORE PyPI publish (irreversible) rather than only at the\n  live registry's remote validation after publish. This wiring is IN scope for this ticket -- the\n  guard function must have a real runner, not just unit-test coverage.\n- Attest (as a ticket comment, once the fix lands) the run URL/timestamp of the successful re-run\n  of release.yml run 33273822041's \"Publish to MCP Registry\" job -- this is an external,\n  point-in-time confirmation and is recorded as evidence, not a codebase acceptance criterion.\n\n## File impact\n- server.json — shorten top-level description field to satisfy the MCP registry's <= 100 char schema\n- scripts/release_guards.py — add check_mcp_registry_description guard + CLI subcommand\n- tests/unit/test_release_guards.py — unit test for the new guard\n- .github/workflows/release.yml — wire the new guard into the Authorize release source job\n\n## Testing\n- pytest tests/unit/test_release_guards.py tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py -q\n- make lint && make typecheck\n- Non-codebase attestation: re-run release.yml run 33273822041's \"Publish to MCP Registry\" job and\n  record its result URL/timestamp as a ticket comment (not gated by an in-repo AC).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] server.json's top-level description is <= 100 characters.\n- [ ] scripts/release_guards.py exposes check_mcp_registry_description with a passing unit test in\n      tests/unit/test_release_guards.py.\n- [ ] .github/workflows/release.yml's Authorize release source job invokes\n      `release_guards.py mcp-registry-description` as a real guard step (verifiable via\n      `grep mcp-registry-description .github/workflows/release.yml`), so this class of failure is\n      caught before PyPI publish in future releases.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The re-run \"Publish to MCP Registry\" job for release.yml run 33273822041 is\n      confirmed successful and its result URL/timestamp is recorded as a ticket comment."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788036890011773001,"uuid":"1a0159b9-7537-437c-9c30-dfd4a8170d54"}